  "description": "A wide driveway camera at 0.5 s cadence, deliberately built around the cases that separate a good setting from a bad one. Frames 0-9 are empty. A car drives in over frames 10-25 and then STOPS for the rest of the clip, so the default Moving Only filter sees the same object flip from moving to still, a still-for-N (dwell) alert has something to accrue on, and a \"car moving only\" zone rule correctly stops firing after frame 25. Frames 28-45 add a dog crossing in front of the parked car, which is the occlusion case. Frames 18-22 carry a difficult, partially visible cat at the left edge that is excluded from the recall denominator.",
